      <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">European Committee for the Coordination of Electrotechnical Standards</skos:altLabel>
      <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Comité européen de coordination des normes électriques</skos:altLabel>
      <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pt">Comité Europeu de Coordenação das Normas Elétricas</skos:altLabel>
      <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/corporate-body"/>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The European Committee for the Coordination of Electrotechnical Standards (CENEL) aimed at analysis of IEC electrotechnical standards to determine to what extent they were suitable for implementation in the EEC and EFTA states. Its members were the EEC countries and on behalf of EFTA Austria, Denmark, Norway, Portugal, Sweden, Switzerland and Great Britain. In 1973 CENEL and CENELCOM joined up to form the European Committee for Electrotechnical Standardisation (CENELEC), which counted Austria among its members.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
