      <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/corporate-body"/>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Intergovernmental Authority on Drought and Development (IGADD) was a multinational body founded by Djibouti, Ethiopia, Somalia, Sudan, Uganda and Kenya, with a focus on development and environmental control. Eritrea joined the organization in 1993, upon achieving independence.</skos:definition>
