      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Group of industrially advanced countries whose central banks co-operate to regulate international finance. The members consist of Australia, Belgium, Canada, France, Germany, Italy, Japan, Netherlands, Spain, Sweden, the United Kingdom, the United States. By the association of the thirteenth member, Switzerland, the name of the G12 remained the same.</skos:definition>
