      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Central African Economic and Monetary Community (CEMAC) is made up of six States: Gabon, Cameroon, the Central African Republic, Chad, the Republic of the Congo and Equatorial Guinea. It presents one of the Central African regional Communities established to promote cooperation and exchange among its members.</skos:definition>
