      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Visegrad Group (Visegrad Four) is an alliance of four Central European states – Czech Republic, Hungary, Poland and Slovakia – for the purposes of furthering their European integration as well as advancing their military, economic and energy cooperation with one another.</skos:definition>
