      <skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/corporate-body"/>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">It is an overall political forum for regional intergovernmental cooperation. The members of the Council are the 11 states of the Baltic Sea region as well as the European Commission. The CBSS was established by the region’s Foreign Ministers as a response to the geopolitical changes that took place in the Baltic Sea region with the end of the Cold War.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
