      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Common Market for Eastern and Southern Africa (COMESA) is a free trade area with twenty member states. COMESA agreed to an expanded free-trade zone including members of two other African trade blocs and it is also considering a common visa scheme to boost tourism.</skos:definition>
