      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Arab League is a regional organization of Arab countries in and around North Africa, the Horn of Africa and Arabia. It has 22 members. The League’s main goal is to "draw closer the relations between member States and co-ordinate collaboration between them, to safeguard their independence and sovereignty, and to consider in a general way the affairs and interests of the Arab countries".</skos:definition>
