      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Bureau is the body that lays down rules for the European Parliament. It draws up Parliament’s preliminary draft budget and decides all administrative, staff and organisational matters. The Bureau consists of the President of the European Parliament, the 14 Vice-Presidents and the five Quaestors elected by Parliament for a period of two and a half years (which can be renewed).</skos:definition>
