      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The European Research Council (ERC) is a public body for funding of scientific and technological research conducted within the European Union. Established by the European Commission, the ERC is composed of an independent Scientific Council, its governing body consisting of distinguished researchers, and an Executive Agency (ERCEA), in charge of the implementation.</skos:definition>
