            <at:legacy-code>TENEA_CRF_232551</at:legacy-code>
         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The European Climate, Infrastructure and Environment Executive Agency is entrusted with the implementation of the following (parts of) Union programmes: Innovation Fund; Connecting Europe Facility: Transport (including military mobility and the Cohesion Fund contribution) and Energy; Horizon Europe: Pillar II, cluster 5: Climate, energy and mobility; LIFE: Nature and biodiversity; Circular economy and quality of life; Climate change mitigation and adaptation; Clean energy transition; Renewable Energy Financing Mechanism; Public sector loan facility, under the Just Transition Mechanism; European Maritime, Fisheries and Aquaculture Fund (direct management) and compulsory contributions to Regional Fisheries Management Organisations (RFMOs) and other international organisations, as well as with the implementation of the legacy of the following (parts of) Union programmes: Connecting Europe Facility: Energy and Transport (including the Cohesion Fund contribution); Horizon 2020: Part III: Societal challenge 3: Secure, clean and efficient energy; Horizon 2020: Part III: Societal challenge 4: Smart, green and integrated transport; Horizon 2020: Part III: Societal challenge 5: Climate action, Environment, resource efficiency and raw materials; LIFE: Climate Action and Environment; European Maritime and Fisheries Fund.</skos:definition>
      <skos:historyNote xml:lang="en">According to the Commission Implementing Decision (EU) 2021/173 of 12 February 2021 (http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2021/173/oj), the European Climate, Infrastructure and Environment Executive Agency is established from 1 April 2021 until 31 December 2028 and it succeeds and replaces the Innovation and Networks Executive Agency.</skos:historyNote>
   </skos:Concept>
