         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Smart Networks and Services Joint Undertaking is a public-private partnership which contributes to the general objectives of the Horizon Europe Regulation. Its general objectives are: to foster Europe’s technological sovereignty in future smart networks and services by reinforcing current industrial strengths and by extending the scope from 5G connectivity to the broader strategic value chain including cloud-based service provisioning as well as components and devices; to align strategic roadmaps of a wider range of industrial players; to advance European technological and scientific excellence to support European leadership to shape and master 6G systems by 2030; to strengthen the deployment of digital infrastructures and uptake of digital solutions in the European markets; to prepare the European smart networks and services supply industry; to facilitate digital innovation; to support the alignment of future smart networks and services with Union policy objectives.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
