      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The European Union Drugs Agency (EUDA) is the central authority on illicit drugs in the European Union. Formerly known as the EMCDDA, the Lisbon-based agency contributes to EU preparedness on drugs through actions that anticipate and alert on dangers, whilst responding to emerging issues and learning from best practice in the field to assess the effectiveness of interventions.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
