         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The European High Performance Computing Joint Undertaking is a joint initiative created in 2018. It pools together the resources of the European Union, European countries and private partners with the ambition of making Europe a world leader in supercomputing.To this end, the EuroHPC JU is procuring and installing supercomputers across Europe. No matter where in Europe they are located, European scientists and users from the public sector and the industry can benefit from these EuroHPC supercomputers, which rank among the world’s most powerful. In parallel, the EuroHPC JU is funding an ambitious research and innovation programme to develop a full European supercomputing supply chain: from processors and software to applications to be run on these supercomputers and know-how to develop strong European expertise.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
