         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The European Union Agency for Cybersecurity, ENISA, is the Union’s agency dedicated to achieving a high common level of cybersecurity across Europe. Established in 2004 and strengthened by the EU Cybersecurity Act, the European Union Agency for Cybersecurity contributes to EU cyber policy, enhances the trustworthiness of ICT products, services and processes with cybersecurity certification schemes, cooperates with Member States and EU bodies, and helps Europe prepare for the cyber challenges of tomorrow. Through knowledge sharing, capacity building and awareness raising, the Agency works together with its key stakeholders to strengthen trust in the connected economy, to boost resilience of the Union’s infrastructure, and, ultimately, to keep Europe’s society and citizens digitally secure.</skos:definition>
      <skos:historyNote xml:lang="en">On 3.12.2013 the label in Romanian was corrected – formerly "Agenția Europeană pentru Securitatea Rețelelor Informatice și a Datelor".</skos:historyNote>
   </skos:Concept>
