      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Europe’s Rail Joint Undertaking is a public-private partnership which contributes to the general objectives of the Horizon Europe Regulation. Its general objectives are: to contribute towards the achievement of the Single European Railway Area; to ensure a fast transition to more attractive, user-friendly, competitive, affordable, efficient and sustainable European rail system, integrated into the wider mobility system; to support the development of a strong and globally competitive European rail industry.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
