      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The United Nations Security Council (UNSC) is one of the six principal organs of the United Nations and is charged with the maintenance of international peace and security as well as accepting new members to the United Nations and approving any changes to its United Nations Charter.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
