      <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://eurovoc.europa.eu/4594"/>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">United Nations Centre for Regional Development (UNCRD), established based on an agreement between the Government of Japan and the United Nations, strives to promote sustainable regional development in developing countries with a focus on development planning and management in the context of globalization and decentralization trends, and the growing concern towards global environmental issues and their impacts. UNCRD is administered by the Division for Sustainable Development of the United Nations Department of Economic and Social Affairs.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
