         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Established pursuant to the recommendations of the United Nations Conference on the Environment. As of January 2015, it is composed of seven divisions: Division of Communications and Public Information, Division of Environmental Law and Conventions, Division of Environmental Policy Implementation, Division of Technology, Industry and Economics, Division of Early Warning and Assessment, Division of Global Environment Facility Coordination. Its mission is to provide leadership and encourage partnerships in caring for the environment by enabling nations and peoples to improve their quality of life without compromising that of future generations.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
