      <skos:altLabel xml:lang="nl">VN-aids-programma</skos:altLabel>
      <skos:altLabel xml:lang="nl">Gezamenlijk Programma van de Verenigde Naties inzake hiv/aids</skos:altLabel>
      <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://eurovoc.europa.eu/8393"/>
      <at:op-mapped-code>
         <at:MappedCode>
            <dc:source>EurLex</dc:source>
            <at:affected-table>FD_050</at:affected-table>
            <at:legacy-code>ONUSIDA</at:legacy-code>
         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Originally drew together six organizations: UNICEF, the United Nations Development Programme, the United Nations Population Fund, UNESCO, the World Health Organization, and the World Bank. The original six organizations were joined in April 1999 by the United Nations International Drug Control Programme. In May 2010 there were 10 organizations involved: the previous seven plus the ILO, UNHCR and WFP. UN-Women has become the 11th co-sponsor of UNAIDS, as per UN-Women strategic plan for 2014-2017. The goal of UNAIDS is to catalyse, strengthen and orchestrate the unique expertise, resources, and networks of influence that each of these organizations offers.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
