      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The United Nations Fund for Population Activities was established as a trust fund in 1967 and began funding population programmes in 1969. In 1987, it was officially renamed the United Nations Population Fund, reflecting its lead role in the UN system in the area of population.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
