      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Commission on Science and Technology for Development is a subsidiary body of the Economic and Social Council. The Commission was established to provide the General Assembly and ECOSOC with high-level advice on relevant issues through analysis and appropriate policy recommendations or options in order to enable those organs to guide the future work of the United Nations, develop common policies and agree on appropriate actions.</skos:definition>
