      <skos:altLabel xml:lang="el">Φόρουμ των κρατών ΑΚΕ της Καραϊβικής</skos:altLabel>
      <skos:altLabel xml:lang="pl">Karaibskie Forum Państw AKP</skos:altLabel>
      <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Forum of the Caribbean Group of African, Caribbean and Pacific (ACP) States</skos:altLabel>
      <skos:altLabel xml:lang="fr">Cariforum</skos:altLabel>
      <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="http://eurovoc.europa.eu/c_acf7832d"/>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Caribbean Forum (CARIFORUM) is a subgroup of African, Caribbean and Pacific Group of States and serves as a base for economic dialogue with the European Union. It was established in 1992. Its membership comprises the 15 Caribbean Community states, along with the Dominican Republic. In 2008, they signed an Economic Partnership Agreement with the European Union, though Guyana and Haiti had expressed reservations and did not attend the signing ceremony.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
